# Diagram Standard — Mandatory for Every Task and Feature

> This rule enforces Section 9 of `CONSTITUTION.md`.  
> See full standard: `docs/diagrams/README.md`

## The Rule

**EVERY** file you create or update in the following locations MUST contain at least one Mermaid diagram:

- `tasks/**/*.md` — always add `## Architecture Diagram` section
- `capsule-projects/*/README.md` — always add architecture diagram
- `issues/issue-*.md` — always add where the concept sits in the request journey
- `plans/*.md` — always add a diagram showing the integration
- `implementation/**/README.md` — always add component diagram

## Required Section in Every Task File

Add this section after the Theory section in every task:

```markdown
## Architecture Diagram

> Where this component fits in the overall request journey:

```mermaid
graph TB
    Client["🌐 Client"]
    %%  Add the component this task teaches
    %%  Show where it sits in the chain
    %%  Highlight it with: style ComponentName fill:#ff9,stroke:#f90
```

**Full project diagram:** [docs/diagrams/00-big-picture.md](../../docs/diagrams/00-big-picture.md)  
**Related diagram:** [docs/diagrams/NN-name.md](../../docs/diagrams/NN-name.md)
```

## When Adding a New Subsystem

1. Create `docs/diagrams/NN-kebab-name.md` with a detailed Mermaid diagram
2. Add the file to the table in `docs/diagrams/README.md`
3. Update `docs/diagrams/00-big-picture.md` to include the new subsystem
4. Reference the new diagram from the task file

## Diagram Type Selection

| Situation | Use |
|-----------|-----|
| Showing architecture or component relationships | `graph TB` |
| Showing a request/response flow | `sequenceDiagram` |
| Showing git branching | `gitGraph` |
| Showing a concept tree or learning map | `mindmap` |
| Showing a timeline or latency budget | `gantt` |

## Highlight the Component Being Taught

Always highlight the component that is the focus of the current task:

```mermaid
graph TB
    Client --> NGINX --> AuthService
    style AuthService fill:#ff9,stroke:#f90,stroke-width:3px
```

## Never Skip the Diagram

- If you are creating a task → diagram is required
- If you are updating a task → add a diagram if one doesn't exist
- If a diagram would be too complex → break it into two simpler diagrams
- There is no valid reason to omit a diagram
